{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>יַקּ֫וּשׁ</b> — a verb, as in 'I set a snare for you'; or an adjective, like 'strong.' The construct is joined to 'destruction,' which is sudden destruction."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 91, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites the root יקש in a verbal form (cf. Jeremiah 50:24); 'destruction' renders הַוָּה, which he glosses as sudden calamity."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:52.186098962Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}